course: dictionary
lesson: 15992
title: Utter: say it, or mean it completely
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Utter is a word with two jobs. As a verb, it means to say something or make a sound with your voice. «She did not utter a word.» She stayed silent, so utter is the action of speaking.
explain: As an adjective, utter means complete or total. «The room was in utter silence.» Silence cannot be half done, so utter means total silence: not one sound.
explain: To tell the jobs apart, ask whether the word is doing something or describing a thing. When utter comes before a noun, like «an utter mess», it is an adjective.
fact: Utter (verb) means to say something or make a sound with your voice.
fact: Utter (adjective) means complete or total, as in «utter silence».
fact: Utter is often used with bad things, such as «utter rubbish» or «an utter mess».
fact: «Utterly» means completely, as in «utterly lost».
fact: The verb forms are utter, utters, uttered and uttering.
exercise: «She did not utter a word.» What does utter mean here? | *To say something with your voice | To write something down | To fall over | To hide something
exercise: «The kitchen was left in an utter mess.» What does utter mean here? | Hungry | Small and tidy | *Complete and total | Very quiet
exercise: «Utterly» is from the same family as utter. What does utterly mean? | *Completely | Quietly | Slowly | Happily
test: The crowd sat in utter silence. What does utter mean in this sentence? | Hungry for food | Full of empty seats | *Complete, with no sound at all | Loud and cheerful
test: Ben did not utter a single word all day. What does utter mean in this sentence? | To shout very loudly | To write neatly | To fall asleep | *To say or make a sound with your voice
exam: Which sentence uses utter as an adjective? | *«It was an utter disaster, and the cake was ruined.» | «She did not utter a word.» | «Ravi will utter his answer at the end.»
